Current original Zero workflow (0.12)

Use the native tools on Linux or their .exe versions on Windows:
  zero-integrate PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_KERNEL.zero
  zero-build PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY NEW_KERNEL.zero
  zero-check PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_TEST_DIRECTORY
All destination paths must be new. The integrator preserves authored sources;
the builder checks its compiler fixed point and builds the original targets;
the verifier checks language behavior and host file operations in process.
See tools/integrate.ztext, tools/build.ztext and checks/README.ztext.
Read these documents with zero-text read FILE.

The notes below preserve earlier implementation and test history. Any old
shell/Python runner names, generated artifacts, JSON reports or commands are
historical references: they were removed from the active project and are not
current runnable instructions or current-release validation. Native host
checks do not replace BIOS/UEFI, persistence or physical-hardware testing.

Historical implementation notes

ZERO WINDOW MANAGER - FIRST VISUAL DESIGN
Date: 2026-11-16 UTC

These are static design previews, not screenshots of a finished window
manager. Sample terminal text is illustrative. They are rendered by the
original Zero program preview.zero, compiled with build/zero --host. The
existing original kernel 5x7 ASCII glyph data is reused; no external font,
GUI toolkit, image, drawing library or guest runtime is involved.

Files
  tiles.png   800x600; one master window left, two stack windows right.
  scroll.png  800x600; focused middle column, clipped neighbors at each edge.
  preview.zero  complete authoritative Zero source for both previews.
  make-preview.py  authoring helper that writes declarative scene records;
                   not needed to compile or render preview.zero.

Palette (0xRRGGBB)
  background       0x0b101b
  top/title bars   0x111a2a
  terminal panel   0x101927
  inactive border  0x2a374d
  focus accent     0xac9ae8
  foreground       0xdce3ef
  secondary text   0x8596af
  prompt/status    0x89d8cd
  window footer    0x0e1522
  active title     0x20263b

Common geometry at800x600
  Top bar y0..57; ZERO brand at18,15, scaled2.
  Workspace row y73; window content region y104..539.
  Footer bar y574..599, hints at18,581.
  Window border1pixel; title bar34pixels plus divider; footer24pixels.
  Body starts16pixels from left,50pixels from top; line advance20pixels.
  Terminal glyphs use8x16 cells; the 5x7 bitmap rows are doubled vertically.
  Focus uses lavender border/title and cyan FOCUSED footer.

Tiled preview windows (x,y,width,height)
  1:16,104,440,436; active.
  2:472,104,312,210.
  3:472,330,312,210.
  Horizontal gap16; vertical gap16.

Scrolling preview windows
  1:-176,104,368,436; clipped at the left screen edge.
  2:208,104,368,436; active, fully visible.
  3:592,104,368,436; clipped at the right screen edge.
  Horizontal gap16; edge markers and PREVIOUS/NEXT hints show continuity.
  Text and borders are clipped to visible window bounds, not wrapped into
  a neighbor. Runtime focus/scroll behavior remains the integration task.

Keyboard labels agreed with the implementation agent
  F1 NEW  F2 CLOSE  F3 NEXT  F4 PREV  F5 LAYOUT
The preview does not handle input beyond selecting which static scene to draw.

Reproduce from project root
  build/zero --host < wm/design/preview.zero > wm/design/preview
  chmod +x wm/design/preview
  wm/design/preview < /dev/null > wm/design/tiles.ppm
  printf s | wm/design/preview > wm/design/scroll.ppm
The source writes standard P6 RGB,800x600,1440015bytes including header.
PNG files were made by external host format conversion for review only:
  convert wm/design/tiles.ppm wm/design/tiles.png
  convert wm/design/scroll.ppm wm/design/scroll.png
No host conversion tool becomes part of the OS.

Both previews compiled and rendered successfully and were visually checked.
They make no claim about runtime multitasking, layout algorithms, memory
allocation, window limits, filesystem isolation, keyboard routing or boot.
